  "problem": "$\\frac{5}{h}\u00f7\\frac{10}{k}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{h}\u00f7\\frac{10}{k},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{h}\u00f7\\frac{10}{k} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{h}\\cdot \\frac{k}{10} & = \\\\ \\frac{5k}{10h} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot k}{\\cancel{5}\\cdot 2h} & = \\\\ \\frac{k}{2h} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $5$ in the numerator and denominator.",
